# GitHub main → Railway production

- After every code change, merge into GitHub `main`, push, and deploy Railway production. Do not wait to be asked.
- GitHub `main` (`asujeff48/Quakers`) is the only source of truth for app code.
- Railway production (`quakers`) is the only user-facing site.
- Railway often misses GitHub autodeploy — after `git push origin main`, trigger a production deploy of that commit and wait until it succeeds.
- Confirm the live site is on the new commit before asking the user to retest. Hard-refresh the Railway URL.
- Never leave a fix only on a feature branch, draft PR, local preview, or one-off CLI upload.
